@startuml
title 1A - Discord: "/jardinero-ticket JAR-58"\nThe command starts nothing itself: it delegates the ticket in Linear

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User
participant "DiscordAdapter" as DA
participant "Store" as S
participant Discord
participant Linear
participant "LinearAdapter" as LA
participant "Orchestrator" as O

User -> DA: /jardinero-ticket ticket:JAR-58
DA -> DA: infer the repository: the one named, the ticket's team, the channel's
return repo
DA -> DA: read the identifier; a bare number is numbered by the repository's team
return JAR-58
DA -> Discord: open the thread the work is followed in
return thread_id
DA -> S: save the ticket's conversation -> thread
DA -> S: create RequestRouter instance
return rr_resolved, subject=linear:JAR-58
note right of DA: born resolved: the subject came with the command

DA -> Linear: delegate JAR-58 to Jardinero\n(delegate=us, owner=whoever asked)
note right of DA
  a ticket already delegated to us is handed back first:
  Linear opens no session for a delegation that does not change
end note
DA -> User: "Received JAR-58. Follow it in #thread" (ephemeral)

Linear -> LA: AgentSessionEvent/created
note right of LA
  the work starts here and nowhere else, see 3A.
  The delivery answers the ask this command wrote, and
  decides which repository the work opens in.
end note
LA -> O: continues in 3A
@enduml
